course: dictionary
lesson: 10091
title: The thermostat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A thermostat is a device that keeps a room, oven, fridge or machine at a set temperature. It senses how hot or cold things are and switches heating or cooling on and off. The dial or screen you use to set that temperature is also called the thermostat.
explain: Look at the clues in «A fever is the body turning up the brain's thermostat to make it harder for germs to multiply.» The brain is changing a temperature setting, so turning up the thermostat must mean setting the temperature higher. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Families also «turn down the thermostat» to save energy and money. Turning down means lowering the set temperature, so the heating works less hard. When you meet a word like thermostat, look for the clues around it, then decide what would make sense.
fact: A thermostat is a kind of control: it senses temperature and switches heating on when it is too cold and off when it is warm enough.
fact: «Turn up» and «turn down the thermostat» mean set the temperature higher or lower.
fact: «A fever is the body turning up the brain's thermostat»: a fever is usually helpful, but a very high fever needs a doctor.
fact: A smart thermostat can learn when people are home and be controlled by phone or voice, so its accounts must be kept secure.
fact: In coding, a thermostat works like a simple «if … then» rule: if the room is too cold, then turn the heating on.
exercise: What is a thermostat? | A kind of cloud that brings rain | *A device that keeps a room or machine at a set temperature | A wooden spoon for stirring soup
exercise: «Families turn down the thermostat to save energy and money.» What does turning it down do? | Turns the lights on | Locks the front door | Makes the room hotter | *Lowers the set temperature
exercise: In the rule «if the room is too cold, then the heating goes on», what is the thermostat doing? | Painting the walls | *Sensing the temperature and switching heating on | Cooking the dinner | Making the room bigger
test: In «A fever is the body turning up the brain's thermostat», what does turning up mean? | Sleeping deeply | Making the body colder | *Setting the temperature higher | Stopping all heat from leaving
test: Why might a family turn down the thermostat? | To lock the doors | To make the house hotter | *To save energy and money | To grow plants
exam: Which best describes a smart thermostat? | A heater that works only in summer | A thermostat that cannot be changed | A kind of clock that only shows the time | *A device that can learn when people are home and be set by phone or voice
